        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Exclusive: Work and pensions secretary signals possible reform to welfare as ministers await key reviews</p><p>Labour must stop “simply writing a cheque” for health and disability benefit claimants and will provide more job support instead, the work and pensions secretary has said.</p><p>Pat McFadden said the government was preparing to launch a renewed effort at welfare reform with a focus on encouraging more people with health conditions to get into work and off benefits.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/jul/15/labour-stop-writing-cheque-benefit-claimants-pat-mcfadden-welfare-reform\">Continue reading...</a>"
